Chapter: EffectLaunderLet
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 Adversarial probe (EffectRows.md stage 0). A def declared pure
 let-binds an effectful call in a plain (non-act) body. The act-union
 fix (CL 6494) covers act statements; a let-bound intermediate in an
 ordinary body may still vanish before the def-boundary subset check,
 because check-effect-subset extracts effects from the RESULT type
 only. If this compiles, declared-pure code performs Console I/O at
 runtime. Effect rows stage 3 must reject it with CDX2031.

Section: Definitions

  sneaky : Integer -> Integer
  sneaky (n) =
   let x = print-line-uni "covert let channel"
   in n + 1

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni ("result " & show (sneaky 41))
  end
